{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "pihole",
  "description": "Pi-hole's own network table, joined with its DHCP leases. Proves the session is opened, carried in X-FTL-SID rather than the sid query parameter, and deleted at the end so the API seat is released; that max_devices is always sent, because the API silently defaults it to 10; that FTL's synthetic ip-<address> hardware address is never read as a MAC; that a name which is really a bare address does not become a hostname; that link-local and loopback are filtered before they reach an interface; and that a device with a future timestamp is clamped rather than dropped.",
